  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>f</mi></math> and <math><mi>g</mi></math> be differentiable functions on <math><mi>R</mi></math> such that <math><mi>f</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>g</mi></math> is the identity function. If for some <math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><msup><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#39;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math> and <math><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then <math><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#39;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to:"
  },
